                <pb facs="0275" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg265"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 6.</seg></opener>
                <head>Consul Archibald to Earl Russell.—(Received January
                        19.).</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> Referring to my despatch of the 23d
                    ultimo, reporting the capture and arrival at this port of the bark Saxon, of
                    Cape Town, I now have the honor to transmit, herewith enclosed, for your
                    lordship’s information, a copy of my despatch of this date to Lord Lyons,
                    reporting the further proceedings in the case of the Saxon, and enclosing a copy
                    of a deposition made before me by the late second mate of that vessel. I have,
                    &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. M. ARCHIBALD.</signed></closer>




